{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqqLFpuJAf6Lp39yQPua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the panic: `Cart.Total()` crashed on any cart that had no discount.\n\n**Cause:** `Cart.Discount` is a pointer, so a cart is allowed to have no discount. But `Total()` read `c.Discount.Percent` without checking, so every cart without a discount panicked. I reproduced this with a test before changing anything; it failed at `pricing/pricing.go:24`.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/pricing.go`): a missing discount now means no discount, and the total is the plain sum. When there is a discount, `Total()` now uses the existing `ApplyDiscount` helper instead of repeating the formula.\n\n**One behaviour change:** `ApplyDiscount` caps the percentage at 100. A discount over 100% used to give a negative total; it now gives 0. I think that's the intended behaviour, but tell me if anything relied on the old result.\n\n**Tests:** I added `pricing/pricing_test.go` with four cases: no discount, 20% off, a discount over 100%, and an empty cart. The no-discount case panicked before the fix, and all four pass now. `go vet` reports nothing.\n\n**Still possible:** an entry in `Items` that is itself nil would also panic inside `Total()`. I didn't add a check for that, because a nil item is probably a bug in whatever builds the cart and a check would just hide it. If the stack trace in production points at the loop rather than the discount line, that's the cause, and it should be fixed where the cart is built.\n\nThe directory isn't a git repository, so nothing was committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1088,"cache_read_input_tokens":24108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1088},"output_tokens":510,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnos